actical guidance.","answerKey":"D","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":3,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"R-B2-003-Q4","level":"B2","skill":"reading","category":"Reading","topic":"work","genre":"opinion_article","audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"R-B2-003","subskill":"argument_structure","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What distinction is central to the final paragraph?","options":["between public-sector and private-sector salaries","between negotiating salary and negotiating benefits","between making decisions visible and making them fair","between experienced and inexperienced applicants"],"answer":"between making decisions visible and making them fair","answerKey":"C","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":4,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"R-C1-003-Q1","level":"C1","skill":"reading","category":"Reading","topic":"society","genre":"analytical_essay","audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"R-C1-003","subskill":"main_argument","difficulty":4,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What is the author’s central argument?","options":["Institutions should avoid major decisions until complete evidence is available.","Reversible choices can be used deliberately to generate evidence before permanent commitment.","Temporary policies are usually fairer than permanent policies.","Leaders should make decisions more slowly regardless of their reversibility."],"answer":"Reversible choices can be used deliberately to generate evidence before permanent commitment.","answerKey":"B","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":1,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"R-C1-003-Q2","level":"C1","skill":"reading","category":"Reading","topic":"society","genre":"analytical_essay","audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"R-C1-003","subskill":"nuanced_inference","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Why does the author compare exit conditions with scientific hypotheses?","options":["to show that willingness to revise a decision can represent disciplined reasoning rather than weakness","to argue that public policy should be decided by scientists instead of elected leaders","to suggest that experiments in organisations produce objective evidence free from values","to prove that reversible decisions have no meaningful social consequences"],"answer":"to show that willingness to revise a decision can represent disciplined reasoning rather than weakness","answerKey":"A","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":2,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"R-C1-003-Q3","level":"C1","skill":"reading","category":"Reading","topic":"society","genre":"analytical_essay","audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"R-C1-003","subskill":"rhetorical_function","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What function does the paragraph beginning ‘There is also a communication advantage’ serve?","options":["to claim that communication matters more than the eventual policy outcome","to reject the idea that evidence can be used in political disagreement","to argue that temporary measures should be introduced without consulting affected groups","to introduce a practical benefit of trials while acknowledging that evidence choices remain value-laden"],"answer":"to introduce a practical benefit of trials while acknowledging that evidence choices remain value-laden","answerKey":"D","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":3,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"R-C1-003-Q4","level":"C1","skill":"reading","category":"Reading","topic":"society","genre":"analytical_essay","audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"R-C1-003","subskill":"author_stance","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Which view would the author most likely reject?","options":["Some decisions require more analysis because they are hard to undo.","A pilot can create harms even when it is temporary.","Once a leader has publicly committed to a policy, consistency should normally matter more than new evidence.","Changing course can be compatible with competent leadership."],"answer":"Once a leader has publicly committed to a policy, consistency should normally matter more than new evidence.","answerKey":"C","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":4,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"R-C2-003-Q1","level":"C2","skill":"reading","category":"Reading","topic":"culture","genre":"critical_essay","audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"R-C2-003","subskill":"nuanced_stance","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Which statement best captures the writer’s position?","options":["Later versions are generally more authentic because they incorporate experience.","First versions should be privileged only when no later version survives.","Different versions provide different evidence, so chronological priority alone cannot determine authenticity.","The concept of authenticity is too subjective to have any useful role in interpretation."],"answer":"Different versions provide different evidence, so chronological priority alone cannot determine authenticity.","answerKey":"C","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":1,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"R-C2-003-Q2","level":"C2","skill":"reading","category":"Reading","topic":"culture","genre":"critical_essay","audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"R-C2-003","subskill":"subtle_implication","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What is implied by the phrase ''an archive’s accidents''?","options":["Digital archives are less reliable than physical collections because they contain too much information.","Archivists frequently damage early drafts while attempting to preserve them.","Creators deliberately hide preliminary versions to increase the value of later ones.","Surviving records may make a version appear earliest even when earlier stages have disappeared."],"answer":"Surviving records may make a version appear earliest even when earlier stages have disappeared.","answerKey":"D","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":2,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"R-C2-003-Q3","level":"C2","skill":"reading","category":"Reading","topic":"culture","genre":"critical_essay","audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"R-C2-003","subskill":"rhetorical_structure","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Why does the writer discuss both beneficial and harmful revision?","options":["to show that the effects of revision must be judged rather than assumed from chronology","to argue that artists revise for better reasons than institutions do","to demonstrate that early drafts are usually more innovative than finished works","to suggest that revision shou