ems once growing debts disappeared.","The library shortened all loan periods at the same time.","Books from poorer areas were collected directly from homes."],"answer":"People may have felt more comfortable returning items once growing debts disappeared.","answerKey":"B","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":3,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"L-B2-003-Q4","level":"B2","skill":"listening","category":"Listening","topic":"society","genre":null,"audience":"general","taskletExternalId":"L-B2-003","subskill":"argument","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"listening","prompt":"What assumption does Daniel question at the end?","options":["that a daily financial penalty necessarily encourages the desired return behaviour","that libraries should collect data about policy changes","that public services need rules that are easy to understand","that reminders can help borrowers remember due dates"],"answer":"that a daily financial penalty necessarily encourages the desired return behaviour","answerKey":"A","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":4,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"L-C1-003-Q1","level":"C1","skill":"listening","category":"Listening","topic":"technology","genre":null,"audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"L-C1-003","subskill":"main_argument","difficulty":4,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"listening","prompt":"What is the researcher primarily interested in?","options":["whether predictive text influences formulation while ideas are still being expressed","whether predictive systems contain more spelling errors than dictionaries","whether people can learn to type without any automated assistance","whether email templates are replacing other forms of workplace communication"],"answer":"whether predictive text influences formulation while ideas are still being expressed","answerKey":"A","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":1,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"L-C1-003-Q2","level":"C1","skill":"listening","category":"Listening","topic":"technology","genre":null,"audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"L-C1-003","subskill":"nuanced_inference","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"listening","prompt":"Why does the researcher mention suggestions that users reject?","options":["to show that rejected suggestions are stored and used to retrain the system","to suggest that merely seeing an option may influence which alternatives feel readily available","to argue that prediction fails because most users ignore its recommendations","to show that writers remember rejected phrases better than accepted ones"],"answer":"to suggest that merely seeing an option may influence which alternatives feel readily available","answerKey":"B","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":2,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"L-C1-003-Q3","level":"C1","skill":"listening","category":"Listening","topic":"technology","genre":null,"audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"L-C1-003","subskill":"speaker_attitude","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"listening","prompt":"How does the researcher view comparisons with dictionaries?","options":["They prove predictive text is simply another harmless writing tool.","They are irrelevant because dictionaries no longer influence writing.","They show that all writing technologies should be evaluated in the same way.","They are useful but overlook the continuous and proactive nature of prediction."],"answer":"They are useful but overlook the continuous and proactive nature of prediction.","answerKey":"D","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":3,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"L-C1-003-Q4","level":"C1","skill":"listening","category":"Listening","topic":"technology","genre":null,"audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"L-C1-003","subskill":"implication","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"listening","prompt":"What does the researcher mean by saying “ease is doing part of the deciding”?","options":["Writers become unable to make decisions once prediction is enabled.","Predictive systems deliberately choose ideas on behalf of users.","Convenient suggestions can subtly shape choices without fully determining them.","Efficient writing always reduces the originality of the final text."],"answer":"Convenient suggestions can subtly shape choices without fully determining them.","answerKey":"C","rubric":null,"sourceMaterial":null,"responseConstraints":null,"primaryEvidence":null,"taskletPosition":4,"bankVersion":"pilot-0.2","qualityStatus":"approved_for_pilot","psychometricStatus":"uncalibrated"},{"externalId":"L-C2-003-Q1","level":"C2","skill":"listening","category":"Listening","topic":"science","genre":null,"audience":"adult","taskletExternalId":"L-C2-003","subskill":"nuanced_stance","difficulty":5,"taskType":"multiple_choice","questionType":"listening","prompt":"What distinction is central to Morris’s argument?","options":["between disagreement caused by ignorance and disagreement caused by dishonesty","between scientific disagreement and all forms of political disagreement","between experts who communicate confidently and experts who avoid public debate","between disagreement that exposes assumptions and disagreement that simply signals unresolved failure"],"answer":"between dis